ck is a hardened and more  violent vigilante even taking to  branding criminals and he works alone  with the help of alfred when we see the  bad cave one of its more haunting pieces  is a damaged robin costume in a glass  case with hahaha jokes on you batman  spray painted across the front there are  bullet holes in the suit but there's  little in the film to explain its  backstory we know a few key pieces of  backstory from subsequent comments and  films harley quinn's introduction in  suicide squad lists her as an accomplice  to robin's murder this admittedly causes  problems for the intended timelines of  both snyder and suicide squad director  david ayer joker has his gold grill in  his mouth upon meeting harley but it is  said to have appeared as a result of  batman beating him in retaliation for  robin's death if that's the case when  and how did the joker actually kill  robin and what was harley's actual  relation to that crime  talking about the lack of clarity over  robin's death in the dc eu highlights  exactly how little we know about  batman's 20-year history of fighting  crime in gotham in a telling line to  alfred bruce wayne laments 20 years in  gotham afrin  we've seen what promises are worth  how many good guys are left  how many stayed that way the line  suggests that fellow vigilantes have  fallen like robin and perhaps turn to  crime in suicide squad we see killer  croc and watch the caped crusader chase  joker and harley quinn and elsewhere  intervene to capture deadshot but other  than some big generalities we know  almost nothing about batman's history in  gotham or with these villains nor the  vigilantes that have supported his  crusade plus most of the dceu has moved  on instead of clarifying any of these  emissions what's the history of this  batman and his allies and conflicts how  did it contribute toward his actions in  batman vs superman you're out of your  mind bruce wayne  in justice league we see the first war  between earth's forces and the forces of  darkseid that took place 5 000 years ago  regardless of the version both showed a  green lantern fighting alongside earth's  forces then dying in the battle with its  power ring flying off to find a new  lantern lanterns essentially protect  sectors of space and will intervene in  situations on a planet they specialize  in protecting from extraterrestrial  threats invasions and other space-based  attackers most importantly sectors  shouldn't go without a protector which  is why the ring sought a new lantern  immediately so where were the lanterns  over the last 5 000 years where were the  lanterns when zod and the kryptonians  attacked earth in man of steel where  were they when doomsday emerged in  batman vs superman or especially in  justice league when another  extraterrestrial invasion occurred these  are exactly the sorts of interstellar  conflicts that green lanterns are  supposed to respond to and while we see  green lanterns in an upcoming hbo max  series it makes little sense that they'd  set out these subsequent interstellar  assaults  in shazam the dc eu opens up its magical  side in the film the rock of eternity is  said to be the source of all magic as  well as the place where the seven deadly  sins are kept the original wizard shazam  and his seven family members formed the  council of wizards there at some point  in the past shazam gave teth adam later  known as black adam powers in that realm  the conflict pitting black adam and the  unleashed seven deadly sins against the  council of wizards resulted in the  deaths of most of the latter  considerable time passed before shazam  transferred his powers to billy batson  and later billy's own shazam family to  fight the newly released seven deadly  sins and the villainous dr savannah  certainly a lot will be explained about  black adam in subsequent films but in  the comics he began life as an egyptian  slave putting the events that killed  most of the council of wizards  approximately around 5 000 years ago  this is exactly when the atlanteans  amazons and early humans fought the  forces of darkseid in justice league if  the council of wizards were around where  were they when evil alien gods were  invading gods atlanteans and amazons  were all there yet the wizards didn't  show up to protect the earth at this  pivotal time  in batman vs superman dawn of justice  lex luthor played by jesse eisenberg  wages a multi-pronged attack on superman  it involved many steps from blowing up  the united states capital to kidnapping  superman's mom in a moment of  justification he claims that his  motivation is basically being against  the notion of gods on earth he argues  that devils don't come from hell beneath  us rather they come from the sky so  clearly he sees superman as an evil  enemy he also shares his interesting  argument of a divine being if god is  all-powerful  he cannot be all good  and if he is all good  then he cannot be all-powerful  ultimately we aren't really given other  reasons for luther to hate superman in  the comics luther is said to have a long  history and personal vendetta against  him not so here the only reason we have  is luther's supposed disdain for gods  that have power above humans luther's  final plan beyond his convoluted massive  tactics involves mixing his own blood  with zod's body combining the two with  kryptonian technology to create doomsday  the ultra  behemoth that kills superman so his  motivating factor is apparently a hatred  of gods and yet his final plan is to  engineer a god that's more powerful more  animalistic and less subject to human  control that's not what a brilliant  planner would do with that motivation so  what's luther's real incentive for  absolutely hating superman  regarding luther's engineering of the  doomsday monster in batman vs superman  dawn of justice the process makes  relatively little sense lex enters the  genesis chamber of the kryptonian scout  ship using zod's fingerprints and  command key he's talked the wealth of  knowledge from the kryptonian archives  learning of an ancient kryptonian  monster aka doomsday that he recreates  as a failsafe if batman can't or doesn't  kill superman the process involves  bringing zod's corpse into the genesis  chamber then luther cutting himself and  bleeding into the chamber and onto zod  the resultant engineering feat is a  version of the recreation of doomsday  it's an effectively mindless creature  with immense strength at least on par  with if not stronger than superman  boundless rage and some serious  regenerative abilities what makes little  sense is why corrupting kryptonian dna  with human dna made such a strong if not  stronger entity than superman humans  look like kryptonians in every relevant  way but doomsday is larger than either  and looks like neither kryptonians are  massively stronger on earth than humans  are and doomsday seems stronger than  kryptonians despite the addition of  human dna adding human dna wouldn't be  the recipe to make this ancient beast  because it's unlikely that its ancient  kryptonian creator had humans lying  around why in the world would blending  kryptonian dna with human dna not make  doomsday a hybrid of the two thus weaker  than superman it makes little sense in  batman vs superman dawn of justice bruce  wayne is woken from a nightmare by a  vision of barry allen aka the flash he  offers bruce a warning about the future  albeit vague and confusing saying bruce  listen to me now it's lois it's lois  lane she's the key  you're right about him  you've always been right about him  in zack snyder's justice league superman  succumbs to the anti-life equation and  under darkseid's rule lays waste to many  of his enemies the flash we can infer  went back in time to warn batman about  superman's inherent danger of course  this was a plot thread that the dc eu  didn't move forward with so there's a  high chance it will never be fulfilled  and we only see in part where it may  have been intended to go at the same  time the flash sequence still exists  within dceu continuity but it's unclear  how they're going to try to give it  finality and meaning if at all  in wonder woman 1984 the fbi turned to  dr barbara minerva to aid in the  identification of the wish-granting  dreamstone failing businessman maxwell  lord wishes to become the stone itself  it grants him the ability to gain power  every time someone makes a wish through  him he uses this to eventually take over  the white house secretive u.s  communications technologies and  effectively the whole world as he grants  the wishes of humanity all these wishes  come with a cost to their users of  course and it all pushes humanity nearly  to the point of global nuclear war  wonder woman uses her lasso of truth on  lord convincing the world including lord  to end the crisis by renouncing their  wishes but even though there's no  indication that renouncing wishes made  anyone forget the events that just  occurred on a global scale the movie  just sort of moves on if everyone on  earth was allowed to make wishes that  came true causing massive global chaos  that would change human history  civilization and religion as we know it  it would reveal the existence of magic  which is a big deal and publicly  confirmed the existence of metahumans as  early as the 1980s it would change  literally everything in the dc eu but  instead it was dropped like it wasn't a  big deal  that's the truth in suicide squad amanda  waller builds a team of expendable super  villains to go on dangerous missions in  the wake of superman's death in exchange  for commuted prison sentences the main  exception is dr june moon who is  possessed by an ancient interdimensional  sorceress known as enchantress when  enchantress and her ancient brother  incubus moved to take over earth the  pair use magic to turn a variety of  people into their supernatural soldiers  the odd thing about all this is that the  villains here are clearly magical  mystical threats and waller knows this  even still most of the members of the  suicide squad have literally no mystical  abilities or relation to magic this is a  major oversight because the only reason  the team succeeds is due to the efforts  of its somewhat magical members for  example el diablo uses his cursed full  fire form to fight incubus and push him  over a bomb waller knows enchantress is  a sorceress so why send an ill-chosen  team for a magical job was the us  government so uninterested in magic that  they never bothered to have good  contingency plans against magic attacks  and have they gotten any better on that  front check out one of our newest videos  right here plus even more looper videos  about your favorite dc movies are coming  soon subscribe to our youtube channel  and hit the bell so you don't miss a  single one  [Music]

